file tests/doc/laws.sml
  signature LAWS
    para:
      |Laws, as the grammar of `Law:` paragraphs reads them
      |(docs/plans/quickcheck.md, D7): the first piece of code is a law, and so
      |is one after "and" that follows a law; one after "for" or "when" is a
      |condition; "for `x` from `G`" is a domain; "when `f` has no effects" makes
      |`f` pure; the rest is prose.
    val twice
      spec: val twice : ('a -> 'a) -> 'a -> 'a
      head of twice: twice f x (arguments: f x)
      para: `twice f x` is `f (f x)`.
      reserved Law: `twice f x = f (f x)` when `f` has no effects
        law: twice f x = f (f x)
        pure: f
      reserved Law:
        |`twice f (twice g x) = twice g (twice f x)` when `f` and `g` have no
        |effects
        law: twice f (twice g x) = twice g (twice f x)
        pure: f
        pure: g
    val nth
      spec: val nth : 'a list * int -> 'a
      head of nth: nth (l, i) (arguments: l i)
      para: `nth (l, i)` is the element of `l` at `i`.
      reserved Law:
        |`nth (l, 0) = hd l`, and `nth (l, i) = List.nth (l, i)`, for `not (null l)`
        |and `0 <= i`, where `l` is any list: two laws, two conditions, and prose
        law: nth (l, 0) = hd l
        law: nth (l, i) = List.nth (l, i)
        condition: not (null l)
        condition: 0 <= i
      reserved Law:
        |`isSome (List.find (fn x => x = nth (l, i)) l)` for `l` from
        |`nonEmpty` and `0 <= i andalso i < length l`
        law: isSome (List.find (fn x => x = nth (l, i)) l)
        condition: 0 <= i andalso i < length l
        domain: l from nonEmpty
    source:
      |signature LAWS =
      |sig
      |  val twice : ('a -> 'a) -> 'a -> 'a
      |
      |  val nth : 'a list * int -> 'a
      |end
